# Unreal Python rules

> **Rule co-activation:** `pn-unreal` also fires on these Python file globs and provides broader Unreal conventions. `pn-unreal-python` takes precedence for Python API specifics when both are active — they are complementary, not conflicting.

- Enable Python Editor Script Plugin and Editor Scripting Utilities per project (Edit > Plugins > Scripting).
- Use `unreal` module for Editor API access. Python runs editor-only; no gameplay at runtime.
- For headless/CI: use `-run=pythonscript -script="path"` commandlet; load level first if script needs content.
- No absolute paths; use project-relative paths or Editor Scripting Utilities for asset operations.
- Test scripts in Unreal after generating; verify they run in target engine version.
